# Nothing here keeps a file out for lacking an extension. The opening this file
# carried until 2026-09-15 -- `*`, `!*/`, `!*.*` -- was meant for stray compiled
# binaries, and what it did was keep every new LICENSE, Makefile and build script
# out of git without `add -f`, and out of the Ore history with nothing saying so.
# Compiled output lives under target/, which is named below.

# Agent worktrees. These are a checkout apiece, so a blanket `git add` in a tree
# several sessions share would commit a copy of the repository into itself. The
# same applies to Ore, whose .oreignore inherits this file: an `ore mark` would
# otherwise capture a whole worktree, since files with extensions are not ignored.
.claude/worktrees/
.wt/

# Rust
/target/
#Cargo.lock # removed for reproducible app builds, e.g. fe2o3_steel
**/*.rs.bk

# SABER C static libraries (regenerated by fe2o3_crypto/build.rs)
fe2o3_crypto/src/c/lib*.a

# Ozone test artefacts (regenerated by test runs)
fe2o3_o3db_sync/test_db*/

# Logs
*.log

# Source code text file bundles
txtcat_*.txt

# Vim
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
.commit_msg.txt

# OS specific
.DS_Store
.directory
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

.srcat/

# The two Unicode bidi conformance suites are 15 MB between them. They are fetched on demand
# by fe2o3_text/tests/unicode.rs, at the UCD version the committed tables were generated from.
fe2o3_text/tests/unicode_data/BidiTest.txt
fe2o3_text/tests/unicode_data/BidiCharacterTest.txt

# The Ore replica. Its store, its bookkeeping and the git mirror it writes all
# live here, and none of it belongs in git.
/.ore/
